      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T15:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The suggested approach requires some additional (and big) changes. For instance, getRectsForRange method on TextLine will change and so are all the other method that assume a single rectangle around all the text on the line. \nI would say with the amount of required changes we need to think more if there is a simple approach.\nAs much as I like the ellipsis to be in the middle of the line it does not justify turning the entire SkParagraph code base upside down (with the main customer - Flutter - never asking for it).",
      "revId": "983687c95573858330016365ab1998e0c30fc3a3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e50b1f5_481d44c2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8956
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-27T15:10:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that the right approach would be to modify the TextLine after adding the ellipsis to modify the runs that belong to the line (cut off the tail of the left one and the head of the right one). That would stand against any query for the visual order (done by runs) and we will have to deal only with text being split in the middle (and I don\u0027t remember any query iterating by the text).",
      "revId": "983687c95573858330016365ab1998e0c30fc3a3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
